Jean Zay, login node, 2026-09-12.  `KInduceDFS/jz_reproduce/run.sh p19 all`.

This is the first time CERT (portable) has been computed anywhere but the laptop.
recertify.slurm only ever compared ROOT (CNF); the `cert` stage had never run on
the cluster, so the value binding BOTH halves -- the search cube set and the
coverage instance -- had only one witness.  It now has two, on different
compilers and a different CaDiCaL build.

Run as `all` rather than `cert` deliberately: stage_cert reads ROOT_CNF from the
conf instead of re-deriving it, so `cert` alone would bind a RECORDED search root
to a freshly computed coverage hash.  `root` regenerates all 22,876 cube CNFs and
asserts that root first, and `$W` is JOBSCRATCH, purged at job end, so the two
stages must share one allocation.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
